-- title:
--   Index of specialty equals dim_K H¹(D)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, and assume `HasPrincipalDivisors K F`: for every $f \in F$ with $f \neq 0$ there is a divisor $D$ — a finitely supported function from the places of $F/K$ (valuation subrings of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$ itself and with principal ideal ring structure) to $\mathbb{Z}$ — such that $D(v) = \operatorname{ord}_v(f)$ at every place $v$ and $\deg D = 0$. Let $D$ be a divisor. The theorem asserts the equality of two natural numbers. On one side, `indexOfSpecialty D` is the $K$-dimension of the quotient of `adeleSpace K F` $= \bigsqcup_E$ `adeleBdd E`, the supremum over all divisors $E$ of the $K$-submodules of families $\alpha \in \prod_v F$ satisfying $v(\alpha_v) \le \exp(E(v))$ for all $v$, by the sum of the preimages in `adeleSpace K F` of `adeleBdd D` and of `globalSub K F`, the range of the diagonal map of $F$. On the other side, $\dim_K H^1(D)$ is the $K$-dimension of the quotient of the $F$-subalgebra `repartitions K F` of $\prod_v F$ generated by the families $\alpha$ for which $\{v : v(\alpha_v) \not\le 1\}$ is finite, by the sum of `repartitionsOf D` (the repartitions with $v(\alpha_v) \le \exp(D(v))$ everywhere) and `principalRepartitions K F` (the image of $F$ under its algebra map into the repartitions, viewed as a $K$-submodule).
--
--   This identifies the adelic index of specialty $i(D) = \dim_K \mathbb{A}/(\mathbb{A}(D)+F)$ with the dimension of the repartition-theoretic first cohomology $H^1(D)$, so that the two bookkeeping devices for the genus and for Riemann–Roch agree. It is used by the Čech form of Riemann–Roch, by counting results for effective divisors and by the surjectivity statement for residues at a regular prolongation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_indexOfSpecialty_eq_finrank_H1.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_Repartitions
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_AdelicIndex

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

namespace AlgebraicCurve

theorem indexOfSpecialty_eq_finrank_H1 {K F : Type*} [Field K] [Field F] [Algebra K F] [HasPrincipalDivisors K F] (D : Divisor K F) :
    indexOfSpecialty D = Module.finrank K (H1 D) := by sorry
